        "text": "The latency waterfall shows how long each stage takes between when you stop speaking and when I start responding. First, turn detection confirms that you’ve finished talking. Then the language model starts generating tokens, which is the time to first token. Finally, speech synthesis begins outputting audio, which is the time to first audio byte. The sum of those delays is roughly what you experience as “how long before it answered me.” You can watch that update in real time on the dashboard every turn.",
